# Generator recipe: lib/CJ/RL/GXA/G_vsnprintf.v, the program tree vsnprintf_prog (lines 29-91)

## The lines this recipe covers

Lines 29-91 of lib/CJ/RL/GXA/G_vsnprintf.v at commit dde52d349c2c34a82325f0f2f2d973bf87d8c2b4 (blob 7569ce1b31a345335b9ae3213bcbb30b39476c3c,
sha256 c337a4c71e9f250c4e1624a7f5c58b33b81152856259b4c7810ce320cad57aa9): the Definition of vsnprintf_prog, from its `Definition` line to the line that ends
with `.`, that is the `PNode` and `PJ_<op>` lines of the tree. As a file (the 63 lines and a final newline) they have
sha256 742a4b6bacb2d4039dc84b64078c8ae20f8d838b5304cc10599119201eb8be11.

The tree is used at line 115: `Definition PROGAT_CODE_vsnprintf (IMG : RImg) := vsnprintf_prog (sym 0x7f000200) (sym 0x22e18) (sym 0x21738) (sym K_SN_WRITE) (sym 0x7f000400) (sym 0x15f04).`.
The file's Requires name no image: its Section takes `Context {IMG : RImg}`. The unit gives IMG for lib/CJ/RL/GXA in lib/A/RT_IImgA_ok.v (fuzz_command.asan, key map lib/A/RT_IImgA.v) and lib/B/RT_IImgA_ok.v (fuzz_command.asan-ubsan, key map lib/B/RT_IImgA.v). So the pins of this tree are fuzz_command.asan and fuzz_command.asan-ubsan.

## The generator

- ptree_emit.py, sha256 000e02022cc9d7fdc7a84ce4f62959039a57c2c1a13d601880297c2739c408a7. Python 3.12.3, standard library and pyelftools 0.33, no
  network. It reads the function's bytes from the image's PT_LOAD segment, decodes each 32-bit word as the 32-bit
  decoder of the RISC-V semantics (theories/Riscv/Decode.v) does, writes it as the notation PJ_<constructor>_... of
  lib/CJ/RL/Reloc/RProgNotJ.v (blob 64af5199ca0d90beff75c174ed890d361e0be2d3) with Instr.v's operand order and each
  field's unsigned value, writes a jal out of the function and each auipc pair as a term over the parameters (checked
  against RStep.v's jimm21, hi20 and lo12 before it is written), and lays the tree out in leaves of 10 instructions,
  split at len // 2 leaves. Its docstring states every rule. It writes the Definition block only, and refuses (exit 2,
  nothing written) a word it cannot write as a PJ notation, an external address the map does not name, and any
  argument or output that holds a string of the --deny list.
- resolve_keys.py, sha256 f6d960fa05b157fd3c0a0014284b1e1ad5e2b84c56b115f27c2324d09e181aa2. It carries each `sym` key of line 115 to the image as
  IInst.v's tsym does, and names the twin's symbol at each address (for a .got slot: the symbol its 8 bytes point to).
  ptree_emit.py does not read its output: the addresses it prints are copied into the command.

